BT /F2 16 Tf 50 780 Td (5. Written Architectural Justification (1-Page Formal)) Tj ET
0.2 0.4 0.7 rg 50 770 500 1.5 re f
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 745 Td (A. Architectural Choice:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 728 Td (We selected an Event-Driven Microservices Architecture with Edge-Cached SDK Evaluation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 695 Td (B. Two Specific Scenario-Related Reasons:) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 675 Td (1. Asymmetric Workload & Independent Autoscaling:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 60 658 Td (Administrative mutations occur at low frequency (<10 req/min), whereas SDK evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 60 644 Td (traffic occurs at immense scale (>100,000 req/sec). Microservices enable independent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 60 630 Td (scaling of Streaming Services without over-provisioning database-backed CRUD services.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 605 Td (2. Fault Isolation & Blast Radius Containment:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 60 588 Td (Under high stress or database downtime, the critical flag evaluation pipeline remains) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 60 574 Td (fully functional because SDKs evaluate against local memory and Redis caches.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 540 Td (C. Security Advantage:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 522 Td (The API Gateway enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and MFA on write paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 508 Td (Internal microservices communicate over mutual TLS (mTLS) with identity tokens, isolating) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 494 Td (sensitive production override rules from publicly accessible SDK endpoints.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 50 460 Td (D. Performance Benefit:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 442 Td (Using local in-memory SDK cached evaluation updated via Server-Sent Events (SSE),) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 428 Td (evaluations execute in <1ms without network overhead, and global rollout changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50 414 Td (propagate across distributed fleets in <2 seconds without database bottlenecks.) Tj ET
0.9 0.9 0.9 rg 50 375 500 1 re f
